course: dictionary
lesson: 3054
title: Eater and the words it joins
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eater comes from the word eat. The ending -er means a person or animal that does the action, so an eater is someone or something that eats. «She is a fussy eater.» A fussy eater is a person who refuses many foods.
explain: The word before eater tells you what kind of eater it is. «A big eater» eats a lot of food. «A slow eater» takes a long time over each meal. Ask yourself: what does this eater eat, or how does it eat?
explain: Eater can also join another word to name an animal that eats one kind of food. An anteater eats ants, a meat-eater eats meat, and a plant-eater eats plants. The first part is the clue, so read it first.
fact: Eater means a person or animal that eats.
fact: «A fussy eater» refuses many foods, and «a healthy eater» chooses good food.
fact: Scientists group animals by what they eat: plant-eaters are herbivores, meat-eaters are carnivores, and animals that eat both are omnivores.
fact: A panda has a meat-eater's gut, so it gets little goodness from bamboo and must eat a huge amount.
fact: In a food chain, the arrows point from the food to the eater.
exercise: «The fossa is Madagascar's biggest meat-eater.» What does meat-eater mean? | An animal that eats plants | *An animal that eats meat | Dangerous hunter that lives in trees | A person who cooks meat
exercise: Jayden says, «What is a fussy eater?» What is the answer? | *A person who refuses many foods | A person who eats very quickly | A person who cooks dinner for the family | A person who eats only at night
exercise: In a food chain, grass, rabbit, fox, which way do the arrows point? | Up and down the chain | *From the food to the eater | They do not point anywhere | From the eater to the food
test: What does «anteater» mean? | A small ant that lives in a nest | *An animal that eats ants | A fussy eater who likes ants | An animal that eats plants
test: «A healthy eater chooses which kind of food?» | Food that someone else has chosen | Food that is very big | Sweets and crisps only | *Good food
exam: In «a plant-eater», what does the word plant tell you? | It tells you what the animal eats | It tells you where the animal sleeps | It tells you how old the animal is | *It tells you the animal's colour
